    "change": "In the sources, the elapsed time of each sample is known, and the flow is fitted offline or learned by gradient descent across trajectories. Four things change here.\n(1) Each demonstration is treated as a sample of one unknown flow at an unknown integer duration e in {1..M}. The duration is inferred online by comparing the observed successor lift v with the orbit z_c = (K^T)^c u of the current in-context operator.\n(2) The operator is identified in context by recursive least squares. A duration-e sample is written as the exact one-step pair (Phi[j], v), where j is the token nearest to the transported orbit point z_{e-1}. This couples identification and duration inference without accumulating error.\n(3) The duration is set to 1 while the pair lies in unidentified directions, which bootstraps the flow.\n(4) Prediction runs the flow for the most recently inferred duration and decodes through the tied lift.\nThe error accumulation from 2605.00836 is used only for the precondition E_M < mu.",
